@@ -70,6 +70,23 @@ The :meth:`~rich.console.Console.log` methods offers the same capabilities as pr
 To help with debugging, the log() method has a ``log_locals`` parameter. If you set this to ``True``, Rich will display a table of local variables where the method was called.
 
 
+Low level output
+----------------
+
+The :meth:`~rich.console.Console.out` method is a lower-level alternative to print and log. It converts each object with ``str()``, joins them with ``sep``, and writes the result followed by ``end``. Here's an example::
+
+    console.out("Hello", "World", sep=", ", style="bold")
+
+``out`` does the following:
+
+* Writes plain text, without pretty printing of containers.
+* Does not wrap, crop, or apply markup or emoji codes; text such as ``[bold]`` or ``:smiley:`` is written literally.
+* Applies highlighting by default. Set ``highlight=False`` to disable it, or ``highlight=None`` to use the Console's highlight setting.
+* Applies a basic ``style`` in the same way as print.
+
+Output still goes through the normal print path, so render hooks, buffering, and capturing work as they do for print.
+
+
